<title>REPUBLIC OF IRELAND: Sigma Wireless 3.7mln punt expansion makes 75 jobs.</title>
<headline>Sigma Wireless 3.7mln punt expansion makes 75 jobs.</headline>
<dateline>DUBLIN 1997-04-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ireland's Minister for Enterprise and Employment Richard Bruton said on Monday that a 3.7 million punt expansion plan by Sigma Wireless Technologies Ltd would create 75 new jobs.</p>
<p>The expansion plan, backed by Forbairt, a state-owned body which promotes indigenous industry development, will result in an increase in manufacturing capacity, further investment in research and development and increased overseas market support, Bruton said in a statement.</p>
<p>Sigma, a unit of Sigma Communications Group, designs and manufactures a range of antennas and accessories for mobile phone and radio industry.</p>
<p>-- Dublin newsroom + 353 1 676 9775</p>
